s overrides inherited disabling":"Wrong; removeAttribute affects only the element's own attribute, not the fieldset's independent disabling."}},{"index":2,"valid":true,"answer":"willValidate is false; checkValidity() returns true","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A disabled input is barred from constraint validation, so willValidate is false. checkValidity() returns false only when the element is a candidate that fails its constraints; a barred element is not a candidate, so it returns true regardless of the invalid value.","choiceExplanations":{"willValidate is true; checkValidity() returns false":"Wrong on both counts; the input is barred, so willValidate is false and checkValidity does not perform validation.","willValidate is true; checkValidity() returns true":"Wrong because willValidate must be false for a disabled (barred) input.","willValidate is false; checkValidity() returns true":"Correct: barred from validation means willValidate is false and checkValidity() vacuously returns true.","willValidate is false; checkValidity() returns false":"Wrong because checkValidity() returns false only for candidates that fail; a barred control returns true."}}]}
